{% block subject %}MonadCount beta: an invitation{% endblock %}
{% block body %}
Hi {{ name ?? 'there' }},

thanks for signing up for the MonadCount student beta. I can include you in the next round.

MonadCount investigates how Wi-Fi and Bluetooth measurements can help us understand how busy a room is. The companion app runs a short measurement task at FIIT, and what I need from you is to try it and tell me how the app behaved. No experience with wireless sensing is needed. Bugs are welcome; they were probably coming anyway.

There is nothing to install yet. A tester link for your phone ({{ platform }}) follows in a separate message once your place is confirmed.

What to expect:
- Time: [expected time for this task]
- Data recorded during the task: [what this task records]. What the app itself records is described in the privacy policy: {{ privacy_url }}
- Where: FIIT STU, Bratislava. If you said you could only test remotely, I will say what is possible from home.

Reply to this message if you would like to take part, or if your plans have changed. Questions go to jakub.dubec@stuba.sk.

Jakub Dubec
FIIT STU Bratislava
{% endblock %}
